From: substrate
Subject: kdrive linux: put keyboard into K_RAW alongside KD_GRAPHICS

Xfbdev's evdev keyboard backend reads /dev/input/eventN directly and
never calls KDSKBMODE itself -- only the legacy LinuxKeyboardDriver
does.  When launched from a shell the kernel TTY line discipline
keeps feeding keystrokes to the shell behind the X session, so
typing echoes onto the framebuffer and never reaches X clients.

Issue KDSKBMODE(K_RAW) right after KDSETMODE(KD_GRAPHICS) in
LinuxEnable, which runs regardless of which input driver is
selected.  Non-fatal on failure (older kernels without the ioctl).

--- a/hw/kdrive/linux/linux.c
+++ b/hw/kdrive/linux/linux.c
@@ -260,6 +260,13 @@
     if (ioctl(LinuxConsoleFd, KDSETMODE, KD_GRAPHICS) < 0) {
         FatalError("LinuxInit: KDSETMODE KD_GRAPHICS failed\n");
     }
+    /* Put the keyboard into K_RAW so the kernel TTY stops feeding
+     * keystrokes to the shell that launched us.  The evdev keyboard
+     * backend reads events directly from /dev/input/eventN and does
+     * not call KDSKBMODE itself -- only the legacy LinuxKeyboard
+     * backend does.  Without this, every key the user types is
+     * echoed by the shell behind X. */
+    (void)ioctl(LinuxConsoleFd, KDSKBMODE, K_RAW);
     enabled = TRUE;
 }
 
